vaulthalla (1.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Security
    - One authorization path for CLI and web: users, roles, groups, vaults,
      API keys, the S3 gateway, price budgets and settings run through shared
      core/ops operations instead of two diverging implementations.
    - Close role escalation: admin accounts are judged by what their role
      grants, nobody assigns or manages a role above their own, and the super
      admin can't be renamed or have its password reset by others.
    - Deleting, deactivating, re-roling or resetting an account ends its
      sessions; deactivated accounts can't log in; revoked refresh tokens no
      longer rehydrate sessions; logins no longer read a stale user cache.
    - Refuse SQL in `--sort` on list commands.
    - S3 gateway: role grants can't exceed the principal or delegate role
      administration without admin rights; overrides need an explicit effect
      and pattern; bucket existence is not revealed before authorization;
      vault names never resolve to another owner's vault by accident.
    - Price budgets need vault edit permission (owners can't drop an imposed
      budget); settings writes are validated on every surface.
  * Runtime
    - Vault updates reach the live engine immediately; owner changes need
      create permission for the new owner; key changes need Consume.
    - Health status takes a live database probe, so the web console and
      `vh status` agree when PostgreSQL is down.
    - Login rate limiting sees real client addresses behind nginx (#125).
    - WebSocket handlers run on several threads, so login bursts no longer
      stall every handshake (#132).
    - Changing s3_gateway.enabled through settings restarts the gateway.
  * CLI
    - Unknown options are rejected instead of silently ignored.
    - Role permission flags, `role admin create --from` and vault role
      overrides work as documented.
    - `vh user update --disable|--enable`; `vh user create` creates the
      default vault like the web console.
  * Web console
    - Encryption waiver confirmation for S3 vault changes over existing data.
    - Role permission editing applies the full permission set.

 -- Cooper Larson <cooper@valkyrianlabs.com>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 13:59:38 +0000

vaulthalla (1.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Runtime
    - Fix DB pool slot leak that wedged the daemon (FUSE, CLI, apt) forever
      after a PostgreSQL restart; reconnect with backoff, bounded acquire,
      database health in `vh status` (#97).
    - Fix 1.5.x -> 1.6.x upgrade crash loop: accept reviewed historical
      checksums for migrations edited after shipping (020, 060, 082) and add
      097 forward migration; guard shipped migrations against edits (#98).
  * Packaging
    - Maintainer scripts never touch the FUSE mount (mountinfo probe) and bound
      every systemctl/psql call; prerm waits for the daemon to really stop
      (#99, #100).
    - Purge succeeds when /var/lib/vaulthalla is a mount point and gives
      post-purge DB cleanup commands that work without `vh` (#100).
    - Detect an orphaned DB on (re)install: auto-adopt empty DBs, otherwise
      prompt adopt/overwrite/abort (VH_EXISTING_DB_ACTION when
      noninteractive); fix `vh teardown db`; `vh setup db` reports honestly
      and supports --adopt/--overwrite (#101).
    - nginx site now serves on stock Ubuntu nginx (unmodified distro default
      site is disabled on fresh install and restored on purge/teardown) (#102).
    - Default config ships under /usr/share/vaulthalla/config and is installed
      to /etc only if missing (no conffile prompts); fresh installs bind
      websocket/preview to 127.0.0.1 (#103, #104).
    - Installs without a TPM/swtpm or without running systemd defer instead of
      failing; opt-outs persist across upgrades; reinstall after remove
      restores units (#105, #106).
    - Depends on fuse3 and python3; Wants= instead of Requires= postgresql;
      StartLimit on units; drop static libs/headers, duplicate udev rule and
      dh_make leftovers (#107).
  * Security and CLI
    - Enforce the default admin password change server-side and rate-limit
      auth.login (#103).
    - Block CLI self role changes and role-create overwrites of existing or
      built-in roles (#108, #109).
    - CLI socket server serves clients concurrently with timeouts; `vh` fails
      fast with actionable errors; `vh status` exits non-zero when degraded
      (#110, #111).
    - Stop shipping vaulthalla-cli.socket/.service, whose orphaned listener
      could hang every `vh` call; upgrades stop and purge them (#110).
    - Web "Edit User" now edits the selected user (it modified the calling
      admin); users can no longer rebind their own Linux UID (#126).
    - A failing WebSocket handshake or protocol handler no longer aborts the
      daemon; an undecryptable JWT secret (DB adopted after purge) is
      regenerated; websocket sessions no longer crash the daemon under
      connection churn (writes wait for the handshake, the stream outlives
      pending operations, close never overlaps a write) (#127, #129).
    - Web console "Add User" works: the user's default vault is created with
      an owner and sync policy, and a failed registration is rolled back
      (#131).
    - Deleting a user who owns a vault no longer prevents the daemon from
      starting (ownerless vaults load as N/A) (#133).
    - Web login works on plain-HTTP installs: the session cookie is Secure
      only when the browser-facing request was HTTPS (#128).
    - auth.login rate limiting counts failed attempts only; duplicate vault
      names per owner are rejected on every surface (#103, #114).
    - A malformed or missing config.yaml is reported instead of aborting the
      daemon with a core dump (#130).
    - Fix daemon crash on unknown group, RBAC on interactive vault create,
      api-key list --json filtering, success reported without state change,
      settings.update, ws contract drift, and secret redaction (#112-#115).
  * Release
    - Run all packaging/lifecycle guard tests in CI with minimum counts;
      idempotent sha256-verified APT publishing with SHA256SUMS; cut-release,
      release-status and lab-smoke commands; scoped secrets and job timeouts
      (#116-#119).

